I got my pet green dragon to kill half a dozen shopkeepers and a priest
easily.  Shouldn't these intelligent monsters have used their magical
abilities (create monster or lightning, say) instead of trying hand
combat?  Just imagine the chaos if I put on a ring of conflict!

Do creatures instantly recognise magical items and are able to use them
appropriately?  I chucked a cursed scroll of fire into a throne room,
hoping that a creature would read it and cause a fireball.
Unfortunately, none of them did.  I've also noticed that monsters use
wands are used correctly; they dig at their feet, make themselves
invisible, teleport themselves, and zap lightning / fire / cold /
death.

Does polymorphing reduce my experience levels or is it random?  I was a
level 30 samurai, polymorphed into giants and titans to move boulders,
and when I returned to human form, I had lost about 100 HP and returned
to experience level 20.  I'm not concerned about my experience levels,
since I have plenty of wraiths and potions to gain level, but I am
curious.

Due to polypiling, I have superb armour and weapons, bags of holding,
amulets of life-saving, and identified almost every item.  I have
finished my quest and now I have found a wand of wishing.  What are
really, really good items to wish for before I tackle the Wizard?

